  "notes": "The federation's own first interfederation supercard, billed on its own air as “the biggest and most star studded Interfederation supercard in the history of the USeW” and drawing its crowd and half its card from five other Summit Wrestling Alliance federations. Five parts survive. Part One — the only one its forwarder tagged [SWA][USeW] — is served under the Summit of E-Wrestling's own wing, where the alliance accession put it; Parts Two and Three, the part labelled “pt 3” and the finale are served under this wing. Four championships changed hands or were defended and two changed hands. One segment of Part Three is REPLAYED footage of an earlier interfederation card — Derek Machismo beating Grim Weibaq in thirteen minutes, and the turn and stable-formation that followed it — and earns no appearance here; that card is not anywhere in the held record."
